  "editorTail": " day. A year and a day. Like a sentence in an old story, like a curse with paperwork.\n\nI came back up by the steps. Ninety-six. I counted them the way I always count them, which is to say I did not count them, my feet counted them, my feet have been right for thirty years.\n\nWind rising by evening. Pressure falling. Wrote it down. Drew no line.\n\nLet the night try the door. The tide was The tide was",
